From: Franco Venturi <fventuri@comcast.net>
Subject: [PATCH] arm: dts: zynq-trx-duo: fcfb PL DMA ring as a u-dma-buf CMA pool

Add the fcfb PL DMA egress ring to the base TRX-duo device tree (created by
0001-add-trx-duo-devicetree.patch) as a page-backed CMA pool plus a u-dma-buf
instance, replacing the earlier no-map carve-out.

The ring at 0x10000000..0x1a000000 is now a `reusable` shared-dma-pool (CMA)
region -- so it keeps struct pages -- and a u-dma-buf node exports it to
userspace as /dev/udmabuf0. This is the Option B zero-copy egress path: the
board server mmaps /dev/udmabuf0, reads its physical address from
/sys/class/u-dma-buf/udmabuf0/phys_addr, programs the PL DMA base (the fcfb
`dma_base` register) to it, and streams UDP with MSG_ZEROCOPY straight from the
ring -- which needs get_user_pages to pin the buffer, hence real pages (a no-map
/dev/mem mapping is VM_PFNMAP and cannot be pinned). The fixed reg keeps the
memory map identical to the old no-map ring (0x1a000000..0x20000000 stays
Linux's) and 0x0a000000 = 160 MiB = the DMA ring size baked into the bitstream.
reserved-memory must live in the base DT: it is parsed at early boot, before any
runtime fpga-region overlay could add it.

Signed-off-by: Franco Venturi <fventuri@comcast.net>
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/xilinx/zynq-trx-duo.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/xilinx/zynq-trx-duo.dts
@@ -22,6 +22,42 @@
 		device_type = "memory";
 		reg = <0x0 0x20000000>;
 	};
+	reserved-memory {
+		#address-cells = <1>;
+		#size-cells = <1>;
+		ranges;
+
+		/* fcfb Stage-1 PL DMA egress ring, as a page-backed CMA pool
+		 * (reusable shared-dma-pool) rather than a no-map carve-out: the
+		 * u-dma-buf node below allocates it and exports it as
+		 * /dev/udmabuf0 with real struct pages, so the AXI-HP0 PL master
+		 * writes here (not cache-coherent), the server mmaps it, AND the
+		 * NIC can zero-copy (MSG_ZEROCOPY / get_user_pages) from it. The
+		 * fixed reg keeps the map identical to the old no-map ring
+		 * (0x1a000000..0x20000000 stays Linux's). */
+		fcfb_ring: fcfb-dma-pool@10000000 {
+			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
+			reusable;
+			reg = <0x10000000 0x0a000000>;
+		};
+	};
+
+	/* u-dma-buf instance exporting the fcfb ring as /dev/udmabuf0. The board
+	 * server reads /sys/class/u-dma-buf/udmabuf0/phys_addr, programs the PL
+	 * DMA base (dma_base register) to it, then streams zero-copy UDP from the
+	 * mmap. size 0x0a000000 = 160 MiB = the DMA ring size in the bitstream.
+	 * option = 0x1020: quirk_mmap_mode[12:10]=4 (PAGE) builds the struct-page
+	 * array so mmap uses vmf_insert_page (VM_MIXEDMAP, NOT VM_PFNMAP) -- REQUIRED
+	 * for get_user_pages / MSG_ZEROCOPY to pin the ring; dma_mask[7:0]=32. */
+	udmabuf_fcfb: udmabuf@0 {
+		compatible = "ikwzm,u-dma-buf";
+		device-name = "udmabuf0";
+		minor-number = <0>;
+		size = <0x0a000000>;
+		memory-region = <&fcfb_ring>;
+		option = <0x0 0x1020>;
+	};
+
 
 	chosen {
 		bootargs = "console=ttyPS0,115200 root=/dev/ram rw earlyprintk";
